{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgacDa2VH7vYz8uE5MG8j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is commit `e7052745` (PR #6145, ticket TRUNK-6646), titled \"Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup\". The bug was in `InitializationFilter`. Environment variables were lowercased and had every underscore turned into a dot, so `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME` became `create.database.username`, which the wizard never reads. The fix adds the credential keys to the set of keys that skip the dot conversion. The commit's diff confirms this for `InitializationFilter.java`.\n\nThe ticket link comes from the commit message and is unverified. The PR data for openmrs-core was not ingested in Falkon, so I could not read the PR itself.\n\n**Lines that implement the fix (current `openmrs-core`):**\n\n- `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS` now includes `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME`, `CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `CREATE_USER_USERNAME` and `CREATE_USER_PASSWORD`, among others. This is the whitelist that the fix extends (`openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java:197-201`).\n- `normalizeEnvVariableKey` returns whitelisted keys lowercased with underscores kept, and converts other keys' underscores to dots (`InitializationFilter.java:1948-1953`).\n- The env-var loop applies `normalizeEnvVariableKey` to every environment variable before merging it into the script properties (`InitializationFilter.java:340-343`).\n- The wizard then reads `create_database_username` and `create_database_password` from those properties (`InitializationFilter.java:370-372`).\n- `InitializationFilterNormalizationTest` checks the four credential keys keep their underscores and that `CONNECTION_URL` still becomes `connection.url` (`openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java:27-73`).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"commit\": \"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 197, \"endLine\": 201},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 1948, \"endLine\": 1953},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 340, \"endLine\": 343},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 370, \"endLine\": 372},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/test/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java\", \"startLine\": 27, \"endLine\": 73},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"pr\": 6145},\n  {\"ticket\": \"TRUNK-6646\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2531,"cache_read_input_tokens":33772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2531},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b8454f9-c398-407f-a39f-c50cb4ae8f70","uuid":"29c4fb99-5585-480b-baa2-d35d9d9f932a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:11:25.533Z","request_id":"req_011CgacDZjNqAEsCqUzw4MfP"}
